    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0638" n="544" xml:id="pg544"/>

                <head>No. 345.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 24, 1887</date>.
                        (Received July 26.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I am
                    instructed by the Marquis of Salisbury to inform the United States Government,
                    in compliance with the provisions of article 34 of the general act of Berlin,
                    that, by a proclamation dated the 14th May last, the whole of Zululand,
                    including the territory known as the Zulu Reserve Territory, but excluding the
                    territory known as the New Republic, and bounded as follows: On the north and
                    southwest by the Colony of Natal, on the west and north west by the New
                    Republic; on the north by Amatonga land, and on the east by the Indian Ocean,
                    was declared to be a British possession under the name of Zululand.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
